# Bedrock repo-local @context — the single serviceable context for every
# situation/<ns>/ vertex (SPINE §4 C3: one @context, no remote loading).
# The registry serves this map at urn:bedrock:context/v1. During the 0.3+
# bridge it also serves a frozen legacy map at the former HTTPS coordinate.
#
# Canonical vertex IDs use urn:bedrock:vertex/<local-name>; canonical path
# pointers use urn:bedrock:path/<repo-relative>. New authoring emits only
# these URNs. Check and context loading remain dual-read for legacy sources.
